1. Applied optimizations: the hot path in [fused_mamba_decode.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/fused_mamba_decode.cu#L174) is now a default-on optimized path selected in [RunFusedMambaDecode](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/fused_mamba_decode.cu#L370) via `NEMOTRON_FORWARD_MAMBA_OPTIMIZED=1`, with the original single-CTA kernel kept as fallback in [FusedMambaDecodeLegacyKernel](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/fused_mamba_decode.cu#L83). The optimized path is split into:
- a grid-stride conv-state update kernel
- a one-block-per-head SSM kernel that parallelizes `state_size=128` across warp lanes and reuses group `B/C` values in shared memory
- a one-block-per-group gated RMSNorm kernel that removes the old `tid == 0` serialized reduction

It also special-cases `conv_kernel_size == 4` and cuts per-block shared memory from staging the full `conv_dim` to `2 * state_size` floats.

2. Double precision: no FP64 arithmetic was present in the Mamba decode kernel itself, so nothing was removed on this path. The `double` accumulation I found is in `Nvfp4RowMajorDot` inside `fused_decode_common.cuh`, which is used by the legacy fused MoE helper, not by this Mamba decode kernel.

3. Compile status: both requested builds passed.
- `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4`
- `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target full_forward_manifest_smoke_test -j4`

4. Expected speedup rationale: the old kernel ran the entire decode step as `grid=1`, so 64 heads and group RMSNorm were serialized inside one CTA. The new path launches 64 CTAs for the SSM work and 8 CTAs for group RMSNorm, so the GPU can use many SMs instead of one. Within each head, the `state_size` loop is now warp-parallel instead of scalar, and the lower shared-memory footprint should improve occupancy further. That combination should materially reduce the current ~0.94 ms per-layer Mamba time even before any deeper tuning.

